EXTENSION "ARMDef_The_Sundered_Eagle_MagicalLandscape_VirtuesFlaws" {
    NAME "Ars Magica Fifth Edition, The Sundered Eagle - Chapter Nine: The Magical Landscape virtues flaws"
    VERSION "0.5.0"
    SPEC_VERSION "0.5"
    RELEASE_DATE "2026-10-06"
    DEPENDS_ON "ARMDef_The_Sundered_Eagle_Core_Ext"

    # The chapter's virtues flaws, structured; each DESCRIPTION the source's text, verbatim.

    #t551fbd35175455a0b862d9 ^"Rebellious (The Sundered Eagle)" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tgA0K9vGShU1WKTibhCc4jXz ^"Flaw"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Printed Name" STRING "Rebellious"
            ^"Size" STRING "Major or Minor"
            ^"Category" STRING "Personality"
            ^"Source" STRING "The Sundered Eagle"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 120
        }
        DESCRIPTION "You react adversely to any attempt to impose authority over you, and work against those who are in command. You do not necessarily have any desire to be a leader yourself, but you don’t like to be pushed around."
    }

    #tce925f0428db229ce004a2 ^"Horrifying Appearance – Snake Legs (The Sundered Eagle)" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tgA0K9vGShU1WKTibhCc4jXz ^"Flaw"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Printed Name" STRING "Horrifying Appearance – Snake Legs"
            ^"Size" STRING "Major"
            ^"Category" STRING "Supernatural"
            ^"Source" STRING "The Sundered Eagle"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 120
        }
        DESCRIPTION "You have no legs, instead your hips give rise to two or more snake-like tails; you should consider how you survived childhood with this horrific deformity. Your movement is not hindered under most circumstances. You can hide this deformity under clothing, but you cannot move without revealing it, leaving you feigning being crippled as well."
    }

    #tf15798146a5b30dd4b3fb0 ^"Folk Magic (The Sundered Eagle)" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tT28cb9EpHcSa3Joedekm2A3 ^"Virtue"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Printed Name" STRING "Folk Magic"
            ^"Size" STRING "Minor"
            ^"Category" STRING "Supernatural"
            ^"Source" STRING "The Sundered Eagle"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 123
        }
        DESCRIPTION "The character is capable of performing very minor acts of magic through his knowledge of scraps of occult lore. Choose one (Realm) Lore that is the key Ability for this magic; he may learn this Ability at Character Creation even if he is normally unable to take Arcane Abilities. The choice of (Realm) Lore also determines which supernatural realm his magic is aligned to for the purposes of aura modifiers. He can only create spells in one narrow area, which must be one of the following four options:\n\n**Abjuration: **Creates a ward against animals or supernatural creature. Uses the Rego Animal or Rego Vim guidelines. **Divination:** Acquire magical senses that detect health, wealth, and mental state. Uses Intellego Corpus, Intellego Mentem, and Intellego Terram guidelines. **Healing: **Grants a Recovery bonus for either wounds or diseases, and aids the birthing of children and livestock. Uses the Creo Corpus or Creo Animal guidelines. Infernal Lore cannot be used to produce this type of effect.\n\n**Evil Eye: **Causes minor acts of mischief like pain, blight of crops, hair loss, sneezing, and so forth. Uses the Perdo Corpus, Perdo Animal, or Perdo Herbam guidelines. Divine Lore cannot be used to produce this type of effect.\n\nTo cast a spell the character must expend a fatigue level, whether the spell succeeds or fails. He must also spend at least 15 minutes preparing the spell, during which time he needs unbroken concentration and access to his “magical” materials (while necessary, these materials offer no benefit to the casting). The spell is designed exactly like a Hermetic spell. The Casting Total is equal to (Stamina + (Realm) Lore + Aura modifier + stress die) / 2. Penetration is calculated in the normal fashion: Casting Total – Spell Level + Penetration modifiers. You may pick this Virtue more than once, to acquire expertise in a different category of spells. Each time you choose this Virtue, you can align it to the same Realm as before or pick a different one, although a character cannot have access to both the Divine and Infernal Realms."
    }

}
